          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The words “Chern–Simons theory” (after
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shiing-shen+Chern"} Shiing-shen Chern
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"} James Simons
            who have their names attached to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+elements"} Chern-Simons elements
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+forms"} Chern-Simons forms
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
            involved) can mean various things to various people, but it generally refers to the three-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+quantum+field+theory"} topological quantum field theory
            whose configuration space is the space of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection on a bundle
            and whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
            of such a connection (for simply connected
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
          %p
            In other words, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sigma-model"} sigma-model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundle with connection
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi conn
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn}
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dixmier-Douady+class"} Dixmier-Douady class
            of this three bundle is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+%28Chern-Simons+theory%29"} level
            of the Chern-Simons theory. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            semisimple this is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
            induced from the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebra"} semisimple Lie algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            For the special case that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
            the theory reduces to the (much simpler)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
          %p
            The Chern-Simons TQFT was introduced in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten89"}> Witten 1989
            ).
          %h2#ClassicalChern-SimonsTheory Classical Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            The properties of the field configuration space of Chern-Simons theory depends on the properties of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+valued+1-forms"} Lie algebra valued 1-forms
            on the given base manifold. Generally, though, it is given by
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ClassicalForSimplyConnectedGaugeGroup"} for simply connected gauge groups
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#ClassicalChern-SimonsTheoryGeneral"} for general gauge groups
          %h3#ClassicalForSimplyConnectedGaugeGroup For simply connected gauge groups
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            we describe the basic setup of
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#LagrangianAndActionFunctional"} Lagrangian and action functional
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#CovariantPhaseSpace"} Covariant phase space
          %h4#LagrangianAndActionFunctional The Lagrangian and action functional
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebra"} semisimple Lie algebra
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle \in W(\mathfrak{g})
            for (some multiple of) its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Killing+form"} Killing form
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            (in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+algebra"} Weil algebra
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            Notice that this is in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgression
            via a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} cs \in W(\mathfrak{g})
            to (a multiple of) the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+cohomology"} Lie algebra
            3-cocycle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi CE
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mu_3 = \langle -,[-,-]\rangle \in CE(\mathfrak{g})
          %p
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            3, write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Conf
                    %mi Σ
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Conf_\Sigma := \Omega^1(\Sigma, \mathfrak{g})
                  \=
                  \\{
                  \\Omega^\bullet(\Sigma) \leftarrow W(\mathfrak{g}) : A
                  \\}
          %p
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie+algebra+valued+1-forms"} groupoid of Lie algebra valued 1-forms
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %strong field configuration space
            of
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth groupoid
          %p
            By means of the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+element"} Chern-Simons element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ←
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi b
                    %mn 2
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi cs
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\mathfrak{g}) \leftarrow W(b^2 \mathbb{R}): cs
            there is naturally associated to every field configuration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a 3-form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi cs
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  cs(A) \in \Omega^3(\Sigma)
          %p
            called the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+form"} Chern-Simons form
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian"} Lagrangian
            of Chern-Simons theory over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          #CSActionFunctional.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              The exponentiated
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
              of Chern-Simons theory is the morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Conf
                      %mi Σ
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\exp(i S(-))
                    \:
                    Conf_\Sigma \to U(1)
            %p
              to the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              to the integral over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
              of its Chern-Simons form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi CS
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CS(A)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi Σ
                    %mi cs
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A  \mapsto \exp(i \int_\Sigma cs(A))
                    \\,.
          %h4#CovariantPhaseSpace The covariant phase space
          %p
            Since the above
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+action+functional"} local action functional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            – which is the space of solutions of the corresponding
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange equation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+structure"} presymplectic structure
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euler-Lagrange+equation"} Euler-Lagrange equation
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CSActionFunctional"}
              are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F_A = 0
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
              2-form of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie+algebra+valued+1-forms"} Lie algebra valued form
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+structure"} presymplectic structure
              on the space of solutions relative to any 2-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensional"} dimensional
              submanifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_0 \hookrightarrow \Sigma
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∝
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Σ
                          %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega(\delta A_1, \delta A_2) \propto
                    \\int_{\Sigma_0} \langle \delta A_1 \wedge \delta A_2 \rangle
                    \\,.
          %p
            The proof can be found spelled out at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/%E2%88%9E-Chern-Simons+theory"} ∞-Chern-Simons theory
          %p
            The statements for equations of motion and gauge fixed Poisson structure appears for instance as (
            %a{:href => "#Witten89"}> Witten89, (2.3), (3,2)
            ) or (
            %a{:href => "#FreedI"}> FreedI, prop. 3.1, prop. 3.17
            ). The symplectic structure on the moduli space of flat connections is discussed in more detail also in (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahBott"}> Atiyah-Bott
            ) and in (
            %a{:href => "#Weinstein"}> Weinstein
            ).
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+structure"} presymplectic structure
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            has apparently first been discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten86"}> Witten86, section 5
            ) and in (
            %a{:href => "#Zuckerman"}> Zuckerman, section 3, example 2
            ).
          %p
            Zuckerman states that on the reduced phase space of
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi GL
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} GL(2,\mathbb{R})
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Weil-Petersson symplectic form
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Weil-Petersson+symplectic+form"} ?
          %h4#WithWilsonLineObservables With Wilson line observables
          %p
            More generally, configurations of Chern-Simons theory are defined on 3-dimensional manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+manifold"} closed
            1-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/submanifold"} submanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi def
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^{def} \hookrightarrow \Sigma
            where each connected component (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeomorphism"} diffeomorphic
            to a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle"} circle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/irreducible+representation"} irreducible
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unitary+representation"} unitary representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi R
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R_i
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            formulation of Chern-Simons theory this means that to the integrand is added the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop"} Wilson loop
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi def
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\Sigma^{def},R, A)
            of the principal connection around
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi def
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^def
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi def
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∝
                  %mo ∫
                  %mi D
                  %mi A
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi def
                  %mo ,
                  %mi R
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi CS
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Z(\Sigma^{def}, \Sigma)
                  \\propto
                  \\int D A \;\; W(\Sigma^{def}, R, A) \exp(i S_{CS}(A))
                  \\,.
          %p
            But more fundamentally, the whole
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop"} Wilson loop
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(\cdots)
            itself here is to be regarded as the result of a path integral for a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 1-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            with moduli space a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbit"} coadjoint orbit
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            and with the representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            arising by the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
            (see there for more details).
          %p
            This means that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
            of Chern-Simons theory over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi def
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma^{def} \hookrightarrow \Sigma)
            is the space of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+connections"} principal connections
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            and of maps to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coadjoint+orbit"} coadjoint orbit
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi def
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^{def}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            now being the sum of 3-dimensional Chern-Simons theory over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            as above and of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/1-dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} 1-dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            along
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi def
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma^{def}
            for which the
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/background+gauge+field"} background gauge field
          %p
            This
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Witten89"} Witten89, p. 22
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#EMSS"} EMSS 89
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"}> Yang-Mills theory
            ) the same formulation appears much earlier in (
            %a{:href => "#BBS"}> Balachandran, Borchardt, Stern 78
            ). A detailed review and further refinements are discussed in section 4 of (
            %a{:href => "#Beasley"}> Beasley 09
            ). Aspects of the formulation in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
            are discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#AlekseevBarmazMnev"}> Alekseev-Barmaz-Mnev 12
            ). The formalizations via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+Lagrangians"} extended Lagrangians
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} extended prequantum field theory
            is in (
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber"}> Fiorenza-Sati-Schreiber 12
            ).
          %h3#ClassicalChern-SimonsTheoryGeneral For general gauge groups
          %p
            If the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply-connected"} simply-connected
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
            on 3-dimensional
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is not necessarily trivializable. (For instance for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(1)
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+bundle"} circle bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            are classified by their
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern+class"} Chern class
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integral+cohomology"} integral cohomology
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^2(\Sigma,\mathbb{Z})
          %p
            Therefore in these cases the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
            of Chern-Simons theory is no longer in general just a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie+algebra+valued+forms"} groupoid of Lie algebra valued forms
            – which is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
            on trivial
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of more general
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connections
            on non-trivial
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
          %p The general formulation of Chern-Simons theory is then this:
          %p
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+space"} compact
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle-,-\rangle
            be a binary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Weil+homomorphism"} Chern-Weil homomorphism
            produces a map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\hat \mathbf{c} : H^1(\Sigma,G)_{conn} \to
                  H^4(\Sigma)_{diff}
          %p
            from
            = succeed "-bundles" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle 3-bundles with connection
            on
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            of Chern-Simons theory is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+holonomy"} higher holonomy
            of this circle 3-bundle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi CS
                  %mo :
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_CS : \nabla \mapsto \int_\Sigma \hat \mathbf{c}(\nabla)
                  \\in U(1)
                  \\,.
          %h4#abelian_case Abelian case
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = U(1)
            the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+group"} circle group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle-,-\rangle
            the canonical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant+polynomial"} invariant polynomial
          %p
            Then the configuration space is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Σ
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}^2(\Sigma)_{diff}
            –
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+differential+cohomology"} ordinary differential cohomology
            in degree 2 – and the action functional is given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} fiber integration in ordinary differential cohomology
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Beilinson-Deligne+cup+product"} Beilinson-Deligne cup product
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi CS
                  %mo :
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mi Σ
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mo ∪
                  %mover
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  S_{CS} : \hat A \mapsto \int_\Sigma \hat A \cup \hat A
                  \\,.
          %p
            (For the moment see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+dimensional+Chern-Simons+theory"} higher dimensional Chern-Simons theory
            for references on this case.)
          %h2#quantization Quantization
          %p
            We discuss now aspects of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of Chern-Simons theory. There are two main formalizations for making sense of this,
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+deformation+quantization"} algebraic deformation quantization
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#GeometricQuantization"} Geometric quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            %li
              %p
                %em
                  %a{:href => "#PerurbativeBVDeformationQuantization"} Perturbative BV deformation quantization of Chern-Simons theory
          %h3#GeometricQuantization Geometric quantization
          %p
            Of the existing formalizations of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            that is naturally suited for obtaining the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+states"} spaces of states
            of Chern-Simons theory and their identification with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+principle"} holographic dual
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states+%28in+geometric+quantization%29"} space of states (in geometric quantization)
            of quantized
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a simple, simply connected Lie group, as
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#ClassicalChern-SimonsTheory"} above
          %h4#geometric_prequantization Geometric Prequantization
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                consider Chern-Simons theory on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} 3-dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
                which is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cylinder"} cylinder
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 3
                      %mo ≔
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 2
                      %mo ×
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_3 \coloneqq \Sigma_2 \times [0,1]
                over a 2-dimensional manifold;
            %li
              %p
                compute the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
                over
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_3
                to be that of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connections"} flat connections
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+form"} presymplectic form
                (as discussed
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Chern-Simons%20theory#CovariantPhaseSpace"} above
            %li
              %p
                after
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+reduction"} gauge reduction
                this becomes a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+form"} symplectic form
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+bundle"} prequantum circle bundle
                on the phase space;
          %h4#GeometricQuantizationQuantizationStep Geometric quantization
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                in order to complete this prequantization to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
                one needs to choose a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
                of phase space; it turns out that one naturally obtains such from any choice of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+structure"} conformal structure
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [g]
                on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Σ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
                (see for instance
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "#WittenJeffrey"} Witten-Jeffrey, p. 81
                = succeed "):" do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "self-dual+higher+gauge+theory#ConformalStructureFromPolarization"} self-dual higher gauge theory – Relation to Chern-Simons – Conformal structure from polarization
              %p
                this is provided by the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Narasimhan-Seshadri+theorem"} Narasimhan-Seshadri theorem
                which establishes that the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+flat+connections"} moduli space of flat connections
                on a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
                is naturally a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+manifold"} complex manifold
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K%C3%A4hler+polarization"} Kähler polarization
                (as well as a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin%5Ec-structure"} spin^c-structure
                for
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+by+push-forward"} geometric quantization by push-forward
                (
                %a{:href => "#FreedHopkinsTeleman07"}> Freed-Hopkins-Teleman 07
                )).
            %li
              %p
                one finds that the resulting
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+states+%28in+geometric+quantization%29"} space of states (in geometric quantization)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi H
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi g
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{[g]}
                is naturally isomorphic to the space of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
                of the 2-dimensional
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
                on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Σ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
          %p
            So for a 2-dimensional
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            of 3d
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory"} Chern-Simons theory
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is naturally induced by a choice
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+structure"} conformal structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_\Sigma^{(J)}
            of the Chern-Simons theory over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            is naturally identified with the space of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+CFT"} 2d CFT
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Σ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi J
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Sigma, J)
          %p
            But since from the point of view of the 3d Chern-Simons theory the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization"} polarization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            is an arbitrary choice, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/space+of+quantum+states"} space of quantum states
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_\Sigma^{(J)}
            should not depend on this choice, up to specified
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence"} equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi J
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
            varies (over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+conformal+structures"} moduli space of conformal structures
            on
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Σ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_{\Sigma}^{(J)}
            should form a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            on this
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+conformal+structures"} moduli space of conformal structures
            which is equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+connection"} flat connection
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
            hence provides equivalences between between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℋ
                    %mi Σ
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi J
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{H}_{\Sigma}^{(J)}
            of this vector bundle.
          %p
            This flat connection is the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov+connection"} Knizhnik-Zamolodchikov connection
            \/
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hitchin+connection"} Hitchin connection
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Witten89"} Witten 89, p. 20
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodPietraWitten91"} Axelrod-Pietra-Witten 91
          %p
            For more see the references
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+theory#ReferencesGeometricQuantization"} below
          %h4#GeometricQuantHigher Extended / in higher codimension
          %p
            We discuss aspects of Chern-Simons theory in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} extended prequantum field theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Higher+Chern-Simons+local+prequantum+field+theory"} Higher Chern-Simons local prequantum field theory
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+space"} simply connected
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G \in \mathbf{H}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+stack"} moduli stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
            (as discussed
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "smooth+infinity-groupoid+--+structures#LieGroups"} here
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo ∈
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_{conn} \in \mathbf{H}
            for that of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} principal bundles with connection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H} =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            for smooth
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-groupoid"} smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+infinity-stack"} moduli n-stack
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundles+with+connection"} circle n-bundles with connection
          %p
            In contrast, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B G \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            for the ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            of
            = succeed "-principal" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization+of+simplicial+topological+spaces"} geometric realization
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group+cohomology"} Lie group cohomology
            we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 4
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^4(B G, \mathbb{Z}) \simeq \mathbb{Z} \simeq
                  \\pi_0 \mathbf{H}^3(\mathbf{B}G, U(1))
                  \\,.
          %p Write
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi c
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{c} : \mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)
          %p
            for a morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}
            representing this class. This modulates the
            = succeed "=" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-group"} cicle 3-group
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+%E2%88%9E-bundle"} principal ∞-bundle
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi c
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mn 3
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  P
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}G &amp;\stackrel{\mathbf{c}}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)
                  }
          %p
            sometimes called the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+circle+3-bundle"} Chern-Simons circle 3-bundle
          %p
            By the discussion at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+String+structure"} differential String structure
            (
            %a{:href => "#FiorenzaSchreiberStasheff"}> FSS
            ) this map has a differential refinement to a morphism of smooth moduli stacks of the form:
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mi conn
                  %mo :
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{c}_{conn} : \mathbf{B}G_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p
            Let then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_k
            be a compact closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \leq 3
            %a{:href => "%28infinity,1%29-topos#ClosedMonoidalStructure"} internal hom
            (mapping
            = succeed "-stack)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\Sigma_k,-]
            and produce the morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{c}_{conn}]
                  \:
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}G_{conn}]
                  \\to
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}]
                  \\,.
          %p
            This in turn we may postcompose with the operation of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+integration+in+ordinary+differential+cohomology"} fiber integration in ordinary differential cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} smooth ∞-groupoids
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(2 \pi i \int_{\Sigma_k}(-)) : [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}^n U(1)_{conn}] \to \mathbf{B}^{n-k}U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p The result is a morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msub
                        %mi Σ
                        %mi k
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi c
                        %mi conn
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mn 3
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi Σ
                            %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mn 3
                      %mo −
                      %mi k
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi conn
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\exp(2 \pi i \int_{\Sigma_k} [\Sigma_k, (-)])
                  \:
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}G_{conn}]
                  \\stackrel{[\Sigma_k, \mathbf{c}_{conn}]}{\to}
                  [\Sigma_k, \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}]
                  \\stackrel{\exp(2 \pi i \int_{\Sigma_k}(-))}{\to}
                  \\mathbf{B}^{3-k} U(1)_{conn}
                  \\,.
          %p
            The result is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/circle+n-bundle+with+connection"} circle (3-k)-bundle with connection
            over the smooth moduli stack of Chern-Simons fields on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Sigma_k
            = succeed "-varies," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transgression"} transgressions
            of the differential characteristic map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi c
                    %mi conn
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c}_{conn}
            constitute
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+n-bundle"} prequantum circle (3-k)-bundles
            for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometric+quantization"} higher geometric quantization
            of Chern-Simons theory, as indicated in the following table.
          %table
            %thead
              %tr
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codimension"} codimension
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k=
                %th
                %th
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+n-bundle"} prequantum circle (3-k)-bundle
            %tbody
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 3
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+string+structure"} differentially refined
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first+fractional+Pontryagin+class"} first fractional Pontryagin class
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/level+%28Chern-Simons+theory%29"}> level (Chern-Simons theory)
                  )
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi c
                        %mo :
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi conn
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mn 3
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi conn
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{c} : \mathbf{B}G_{conn} \to \mathbf{B}^3 U(1)_{conn}
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} 2
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"}
