          %h2#References References
          %h3#ReferencesGeneral General
          %p The local Chern-Simons term as an action functional for quantum field theory appears perhaps first in section III of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stanley+Deser"}> Stanley Deser
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Roman+Jackiw"} Roman Jackiw
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topologically Massive Gauge Theories
              %strong 140
              (1982) 372-411 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.imamu.edu.sa/Scientific_selections/abstracts/Physics/Topologically%20Massive%20Gauge%20Theories.pdf"}> pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/path+integral"} path integral
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of Chern-Simons theory and the relation of its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+line"} Wilson line
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jones+polynomial"} Jones polynomial
            was introduced in
          %ul
            %li#Witten89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Field Theory and the Jones Polynomial
              %strong 121
              3 (1989) 351-399 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01217730"}> doi:10.1007/BF01217730
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104178138"} euclid:cmp/1104178138
          %p and also, indepndently at the same time
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrg+Fr%C3%B6hlich"}> Jürg Fröhlich
              , C. King,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Chern-Simons theory and knot polynomials
              %strong 126
              1 (1989) 167-199 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BF02124336"}> doi:10.1007/BF02124336
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104179728"} euclid:1104179728
          %p
            generalizing the discussion of abelian
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loop"} Wilson loop
            observables previously given by hupf
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+M.+Polyakov"}> Alexander M. Polyakov
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Fermi-Bose transmutation induced by gauge fields
              %strong 03
              03 (1988) 325-328 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217732388000398"}> doi:10.1142/S0217732388000398
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            It derives its name from the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chern-Simons+forms"} Chern-Simons forms
            that were originally introduced in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shiing-shen+Chern"}> Shiing-shen Chern
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"} James Simons
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Characteristic+forms+and+geometric+invariants"} Characteristic forms and geometric invariants
              %strong 99
              1 (1974) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1971013"}> jstor:1971013
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Introduction and review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Geometry and Physics of Knots
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511623868"} doi:10.1017/CBO9780511623868
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (emphasis on relation to
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knot+theory"} knot theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                \:
              %ul
                %li#FreedI
                  %p
                    %em> Classical Chern-Simons theory, Part I
                    , Adv. Math.
                    %strong 113
                    (1995) 237-303 &amp;lbrack;
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1006/aima.1995.1039"}> doi:10.1006/aima.1995.1039
                    ,
                    = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                      %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9206021"} arXiv:hep-th/9206021
                %li
                  %p
                    %em Classical Chern-Simons theory, part II
                    Houston J. Math.
                    %strong 28
                    (2002) 293-310 &amp;lbrack;
                    %a{:href => "http://www.ma.utexas.edu/users/dafr/cs2.pdf"}> pdf
                    \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (emphasis on the
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romesh+K.+Kaul"}> Romesh K. Kaul
                , T. R. Govindarajan, P. Ramadevi:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Schwarz Type Topological Quantum Field Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0504100"} arXiv:hep-th/0504100
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
                \:
                %em Remarks on Chern-Simons theory
                Bulletin of the AMS
                %strong 46
                2 (2009) 221-254S &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0808.2507"}> arXiv:0808.2507
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jorge+Zanelli"}> Jorge Zanelli
                , Luis Huerta:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Chern-Simons theories
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.22323/1.124.0004"} doi:10.22323/1.124.0004
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romesh+K.+Kaul"}> Romesh K. Kaul
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topological Quantum Field Theories: Knots and Links in Three-dimensions and Black Holes in 3 + 1 Dimensions
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "https://www.imsc.res.in/~trg/imsc50.html"} IMSC@50: Topology and Differential Geometry in Quantum Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.imsc.res.in/~trg/imsc50phy/12Marchtalk.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Kaul-TQFT.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"}> Gregory Moore
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Chern-Simons Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.physics.rutgers.edu/~gmoore/TASI-ChernSimons-StudentNotes.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Moore-IntroChern-Simons.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                David Grabovsky:
                %em Chern–Simons Theory in a Knotshell
                (2022) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://web.physics.ucsb.edu/~davidgrabovsky/files-notes/CS%20and%20Knots.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Grabovsky-CSTheory.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li#CattaneoMnev08
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Mnev"} Pavel Mnev
              = succeed "," do
                %em Remarks on Chern-Simons invariants
              %strong 293
              (2010) 803-836 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0811.2045"}> arXiv:0811.2045
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion with emphasis on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symplectic+structure"} symplectic structure
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phase+space"} phase space
            and the expression of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+lines"} Wilson lines
            by the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
          %ul
            %li#AlekseevMalkin
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Alekseev"}> Anton Alekseev
              , A. Z. Malkin:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Symplectic Geometry of the Chern-Simons theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Integrable Models and Strings
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 436
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-58453-6_5"} doi:10.1007/3-540-58453-6_5
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/398944"} inSpire:398944
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/files/f61b4dfd4442520fa61fa585e6f91d54"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            of Chern-Simons theory with its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presymplectic+structure"} presymplectic structure
            is originally discussed in section 5 of
          %ul
            %li#Witten86
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              %em Interacting field theory of open superstrings
              Nuclear Physics B Volume 276, Issue 2, 13 October 1986, Pages 291-324 (1986) (
              %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213%2886%2990298-1"}> web
              )
          %p
            (there in the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
          %ul
            %li#Zuckerman
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregg+Zuckerman"}> G. J. Zuckerman
              ,
              %em Action principles and global geometry
              , in Mathematical Aspects of String Theory, S. T. Yau (Ed.), World Scientific, Singapore, 1987, pp. 259–284. (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/ZuckermanVariation.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p A detailed discussion of the symplectic structure on the moduli space of flat connections is in
          %ul
            %li#AtiyahBott
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Atiyah"}> Michael Atiyah
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Raoul+Bott"} Raoul Bott
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Yang-Mills equations over Riemann surfaces
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/37156"} JSTOR
            %li#Weinstein
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Weinstein"}> Alan Weinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The symplectic structure on moduli space
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~alanw/Moduli.pdf"} pdf
          %p A talk about the historical origins of the standard Chern-Simons forms see
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Simons"}> James Simons
              ,
              %em Origin of Chern-Simons
              talk at Simons Center for Geometry and Physics (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://media.scgp.stonybrook.edu/video/video.php?f=20110728_1_qtp.mp4"}> video
              )
          %p
            A discussion of Chern-Simons theory as a canonical object in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-Chern-Weil+theory"} infinity-Chern-Weil theory
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometric+quantization"} higher geometric quantization
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FiorenzaSatiSchreiber
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/A+higher+stacky+perspective+on+Chern-Simons+theory"} A higher stacky perspective on Chern-Simons theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Mathematical Aspects of Quantum Field Theories
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.2580"} arXiv:1301.2580
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-09949-1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-09949-1
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Rogers"} Chris Rogers
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/AKSZ+Sigma-Models+in+Higher+Chern-Weil+Theory"} AKSZ Sigma-Models in Higher Chern-Weil Theory
          %p
            Relation to Chern-Simons to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dijkgraaf-Witten+theory"} Dijkgraaf-Witten theory
          %ul
            %li
              Thomas Nicosanti, Pavel Putrov, Johann Quenta-Raygada:
              %em
                Approximating
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} SU
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{SU}(2)
                Chern-Simons theory by finite group gauge theories
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.11704"}> arXiv:https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.11704
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %h3#ReferencesWithWilsonLoops With Wilson loops, defects and boundaries
          %p
            The
            = succeed "-formulation" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbit+method"} orbit method
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wilson+loops"} Wilson loops
            in 3d Chern-Simons theory was vaguely indicated in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten89"}> Witten89, p. 22
            ). More details were discussed in
          %ul#EMSS
            %li
              S. Elitzur,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Moore"} Greg Moore
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nathan+Seiberg"} Nathan Seiberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Remarks on the Canonical Quantization of the Chern-Simons-Witten Theory
          %p
            In the context of other
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theories"} gauge theories
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"}> Yang-Mills theory
            ) the same formulation appears much earlier in
          %ul#BBS
            %li
              A. P. Balachandran, S. Borchardt, and A. Stern,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lagrangian And Hamiltonian Descriptions of Yang-Mills Particles
          %p
            A detailed review and further refinements are discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#AlekseevMalkin"}> Alekseev-Malkin
            ) and in section 4 of
          %ul#Beasley
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chris+Beasley"}> Chris Beasley
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Localization for Wilson Loops in Chern-Simons Theory
              = succeed "," do
                %em Chern-Simons Gauge Theory: 20 Years After
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0911.2687"} arXiv:0911.2687
          %p
            Aspects of the formulation in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+formalism"} BV-BRST formalism
            are discussed in (
            %a{:href => "#AlekseevBarmazMnev"}> Alekseev-Barmaz-Mnev
            ).
          %p
            Discussion of
            %em topological
            boundaries (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/branes"}> branes
            ) and suface
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QFT+with+defects"} defects
            for Chern-Simons theory (as opposed to the non-topoligical
            = succeed "-boundaries)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/WZW+model"} WZW model
          %ul#KapustinSaulina11
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Natalia+Saulina"} Natalia Saulina
              %em Surface operators in 3d TFT and 2d Rational CFT
              in
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              (eds.)
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Mathematical+Foundations+of+Quantum+Field+and+Perturbative+String+Theory"} Mathematical Foundations of Quantum Field and Perturbative String Theory
              AMS, 2011
          %ul#KapustinSaulina12
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Kapustin"}> Anton Kapustin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Natalia+Saulina"} Natalia Saulina
              = succeed "," do
                %em Topological boundary conditions in abelian Chern-Simons theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1008.0654"} arXiv:1008.0654
          %ul#FSV
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%BCrgen+Fuchs"}> Jürgen Fuchs
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Christoph+Schweigert"} Christoph Schweigert
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alessandro+Valentino"} Alessandro Valentino
              %em Bicategories for boundary conditions and for surface defects in 3-d TFT
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1203.4568"}> arXiv:1203.4568
              )
          %h3#quantization_2 Quantization
          %p
            We list discussions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization"} quantization
            of Chern-Simons theory.
          %h4#ReferencesGeometricQuantization Geometric quantization
          %p
            The original method of quantization of Chern-Simons theory used already in (
            %a{:href => "#Witten89"}> Witten 89
            ) is
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization"} geometric quantization
          %p More discussion of this is in
          %ul
            %li#WittenJeffrey
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                (lecture notes by Lisa Jeffrey),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em New results in Chern-Simons theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Donaldson"} Simon Donaldson
                %em Geometry of low dimensional manifolds 2: Symplectic manifolds and Jones-Witten theory
                (1989) (
                %a{:href => "http://cs5538.userapi.com/u11728334/docs/06f79688de6f/S_K_Donaldson_Geometry_of_LowDimensional_Ma.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#AxelrodPietraWitten91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
                , S. Della Pietra,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Geometric quantization of Chern-Simons gauge theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.jdg/1214446565"} EUCLID
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
                ,
                %em Geometric Quantization of Chern-Simons Gauge Theory
                PhD thesis (1991)
          %p
            and for the generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+Lie+groups"} complex Lie groups
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantization of Chern-Simons gauge theory with complex gauge group
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://projecteuclid.org/euclid.cmp/1104202513"} Euclid
          %p
            The role of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/metaplectic+correction"} metaplectic correction
            is studied in some detail in
          %ul
            %li#ScheinostSchottenloher96
              Peter Scheinost,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Schottenloher"} Martin Schottenloher
              = succeed "," do
                %em Metaplectic quantization of the moduli spaces of flat and parabolic bundles
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://eudml.org/doc/153753"} web
          %p
            Also, from p. 154 (11 of 76) on, this article carefully discusses what is really the non-abelian version of the Griffiths
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+Jacobian"} intermediate Jacobian
            structure (see there) for
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
          %p
            Detailed discussion with emphasis on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+functions"} theta functions
            and the relation to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weyl+quantization"} Weyl quantization
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skein+relations"} skein relations
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
                %em From classical theta functions to topological quantum field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1006.3252"}> arXiv:1006.3252
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.ttu.edu/~rgelca/berk.pdf"} slides pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Razvan+Gelca"}> Razvan Gelca
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alejandro+Uribe"} Alejandro Uribe
                %em
                  Quantum mechanics and non-abelian theta functions for the gauge group
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1007.2010"}> arXiv:1007.2010
                )
          %p Decent expositions are for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              M. B. Young,
              %em Chern-Simons theory, knots and moduli spaces of connections
              2010 (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.sunysb.edu/~myoung/CS.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p and in section 3.3 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tudor+Dimofte"}> Tudor Dimofte
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sergei+Gukov"} Sergei Gukov
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quantum Field Theory and the Volume Conjecture
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.4808"} arXiv:1003.4808
          %p
            Discussion that relates the geometric quantization of
            = succeed "-Chern-Simons" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reshetikhin-Turaev+construction"} Reshetikhin-Turaev construction
            of a 3d-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/TQFT"} TQFT
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modular+tensor+category"} modular tensor category
            induced by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Andersen12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B8rgen+Andersen"}> Jørgen Andersen
              ,
              %em A geometric formula for the Witten-Reshetikhin-Turaev Quantum Invariants and some applications
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1206.2785"}> arXiv:1206.2785
              )
          %p and references cited there.
          %p
            Discussion in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+quantization+by+push-forward"} geometric quantization by push-forward
            is in
          %ul
            %li#FreedHopkinsTeleman07
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Freed"}> Daniel Freed
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hopkins"} Michael Hopkins
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Constantin+Teleman"} Constantin Teleman
              %em Consistent Orientation of Moduli Spaces
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0711.1909"}> arXiv:0711.1909
              ), chapter XIX, pages 395-419 in: Oscar Garcia-Prada, Jean Pierre Bourguignon,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simon+Salamon"} Simon Salamon
              (eds.)
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Many Facets of Geometry: A Tribute to Nigel Hitchin
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.oxfordscholarship.com/view/10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199534920.001.0001/acprof-9780199534920"} doi:10.1093/acprof:oso/9780199534920.001.0001
          %p
            The “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prequantum+circle+n-bundle"}> prequantum circle 3-bundle
            ” in codimension 3, was constructed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"} Jim Stasheff
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Cech+Cocycles+for+Differential+characteristic+Classes"} Cech Cocycles for Differential characteristic Classes
          %p
            and in codimension 2 (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wess-Zumino-Witten+model"}> Wess-Zumino-Witten model
            ) implicitly in
          %ul
            %li#CJMSW
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alan+Carey"}> Alan Carey
              , Stuart Johnson,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Murray"} Michael Murray
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Danny+Stevenson"} Danny Stevenson
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bai-Ling+Wang"} Bai-Ling Wang
              = succeed "," do
                %em Bundle gerbes for Chern-Simons and Wess-Zumino-Witten theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0410013"} arXiv:math/0410013
          %h4#hamiltonian_quantization Hamiltonian quantization
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Alekseev"}> Anton Alekseev
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Harald+Grosse"} Harald Grosse
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Schomerus"} Volker Schomerus
              %em Combinatorial quantization of the Hamiltonian Chern-Simons theory
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mat.univie.ac.at/~esiprpr/esi079.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %h4#ReferencesPerturbativeQuantization Perturbative quantization
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} perturbative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantization+of+Chern-Simons+theory"} quantization of Chern-Simons theory
            (yielding
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vassiliev+invariants"} Vassiliev invariants
          %ul
            %li#BarNatan91
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Perturbative aspects of the Chern-Simons topological quantum field theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://inspirehep.net/record/323500"} spire:323500
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://search.proquest.com/docview/303979053"} proquest:303979053
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/BarNatanPerturbativeCS91.pdf", :title => ""} BarNatanPerturbativeCS91.pdf
            %li#BarNatan95
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dror+Bar-Natan"}> Dror Bar-Natan
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Perturbative Chern-Simons theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0218216595000247"} doi:10.1142/S0218216595000247
            %li#AxelrodSinger
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Chern-Simons Perturbation Theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9110056"} arXiv:hep-th/9110056
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Scott+Axelrod"}> Scott Axelrod
                ,
                = succeed ",_Chern\u2013Simons" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Isadore+Singer"} Isadore Singer
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9304087"} arXiv:hep-th/9304087
            %li#Kontsevich
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Feynman diagrams and low-dimensional topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.ihes.fr/~maxim/TEXTS/Feynman%20%20diagrams%20and%20low-dimensional%20topology.pdf"} pdf
            %li#LambrechtsVolic14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pascal+Lambrechts"}> Pascal Lambrechts
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ismar+Voli%C4%87"} Ismar Volić
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Formality of the little N-disks operad
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0808.0457"} arXiv:0808.0457
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/memo/1079"} doi:10.1090/memo/1079
          %p
            See also at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/correlator+as+differential+form+on+configuration+space+of+points"} correlator as differential form on configuration space of points
            and see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graph+complex"} graph complex
            as a model for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spaces+of+knots"} spaces of knots
            %em .
          %p
            Perturbative quantization along the lines of
            %em
              %a{:href => "renormalization#OfTheoriesInBVForm"} Renormalization - Of theories in BV-CS form
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Renormalization+and+Effective+Field+Theory"} Renormalization and Effective Field Theory
              AMS (2011) (
              %a{:href => "http://www.ams.org/publications/authors/books/postpub/surv-170"}> publisher webpage
              )
          %p building on results summarized in section 1.11 and 1.12 and discussed in more detail in section 3 of
          %ul#Costello
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Costello"}> Kevin Costello
              ,
              %em Renormalisation and the Batalin-Vilkovisky formalism
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0706.1533"}> arXiv:0706.1533
              )
          %p
            In comparison it says in (
            %a{:href => "#Costello"}> Costello, p. 14
            )
          %blockquote
            %p
              In the case when
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(\mathcal{E})
              %a{:href => "#Kontsevich"} Kontsevich 94
              and
              %a{:href => "#AxelrodSinger"} Axelrod-Singer 92, 94
              (when
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dim
                      %mi M
                      %mo =
                      %mn 3
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim M = 3
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℰ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^\bullet(\mathcal{E}) = 0
          %p
            The BV-formalism for Chern-Simons theory on manifolds with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary"} boundary
            is discussed in
          %ul#AlekseevBarmazMnev
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anton+Alekseev"}> Anton Alekseev
              , Yves Barmaz,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Mnev"} Pavel Mnev
              %em Chern-Simons Theory with Wilson Lines and Boundary in the BV-BFV Formalism
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1212.6256"}> arXiv:1212.6256
              )
          %p based on
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pavel+Mnev"} Pavel Mnev
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nicolai+Reshetikhin"} Nicolai Reshetikhin
              %em Classical BV theories on manifolds with boundary
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1201.0290"}> arXiv:1201.0290
              )
          %p On p. 3 there it says:
          %blockquote
            %p There is a consensus that perturbative quantization of the classical Chern-Simons theory gives the same asymptotical expansions as the combinatorial topological field theory based on quantized universal enveloping algebras at roots of unity (45), or, equivalently, on the modular category corresponding to the Wess-Zumino-Witten conformal field theory (56, 42) with the first semiclassical computations involving torsion made in (56). However this conjecture is still open despite a number of important results in this direction, see for example (47, 3).
            %p One of the reasons why the conjecture is still open is that for manifolds with boundary the perturbative quantization of Chern-Simons theory has not been developed yet. On the other hand, for closed manifolds the perturbation theory involving Feynman diagrams was developed in (32, 27, 7) and in (5, 35, 13). For the latest development see (19). Closing this gap and developing the perturbative quantization of Chern-Simons theory for manifolds with boundary is one of the main motivations for the project started in this paper.
          %h4#as_second_quantization_of_the_a_or_bmodel As second quantization of the A- or B-model
          %p In
          %ul
            %li#Witten94
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"}> Edward Witten
              \.
              %em Chern–Simons Theory as a String Theory
              Prog. Math. 133: 637–678. (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9207094"}> arXiv:hep-th/9207094
              ).
          %p
            an argument was given that Chern-Simons theory can be understood as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+QFT"} effective
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/target+space"} target space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-model"} A-model
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-model"} B-model
            = succeed "." do
